<title>FRANCE: Roussel rises on Hoechst Clariant moves.</title>
<headline>Roussel rises on Hoechst Clariant moves.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French pharmaceuticals group Roussel Uclaf firmed on Tuesday on news its German parent Hoechst AG plans to merge some of its businesses with Clariant AG of Switzerland, market sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;As soon as Hoechst goes up, Roussel Uclaf rises in sympathy,&quot; said one market operator.</p>
<p>Roussel traded up 0.86 percent to 1,412 francs on volume of 49,282 shares at 1421 GMT. Hoechst, which owns 56.51 percent of Roussel, added 3.53 percent in Paris to 240.5 francs.</p>
<p>Hoechst will merge its speciality chemicals business, pigments and additives and other activities into the new group.</p>
</text>
